<title>DENMARK: Goldman Sachs declares Phoenix stake.</title>
<headline>Goldman Sachs declares Phoenix stake.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Goldman Sachs International on Friday announced that it held 5.5 percent of shares in Danish roadbuilder Phoenix Contractors, target of takeover bids by two Danish companies and a Norwegian firm.</p>
<p>The announcement was in compliance with Copenhagen Stock Exchange disclosure rules, requiring a buyer to state if its stake in a company rises by five percent or exceeds one-third or two-thirds.</p>
<p>Phoenix's most-traded C-share closed on Friday at 635 crowns, 7.6 percent above its close on Wednesday, before the latest two bids.</p>
<p>The suitors are Denmark's Superfos and Marius Pedersen and Norway's Rieber and Son.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
